    "body": "CI builds `exhaustive_tests` only for its default group order, 13. The other two orders in `src/group_impl.h`, 7 and 199, are never compiled. Order 7 is the even-order curve, where the ellswift tests are skipped.\n\n`ci/ci.sh` now rebuilds `exhaustive_tests` for `EXHAUSTIVE_TEST_ORDER` and runs it with `EXHAUSTIVE_TEST_ARGS`. A new job, `exhaustive_debian`, has two rows: order 7, and order 199.\n\nA full run at order 199 would take about 7 weeks on my machine: one part in 100000 takes 51 s, of which about 10 s is fixed cost. So the order 199 row runs one part in 20000, using the existing `numcores` and `thiscore` arguments. These come after the seed argument, so the seed is fixed. Every run still builds the order 199 tables and checks the whole group against `ecmult_gen`.\n\nThe first commit removes an unused-function warning that order 7 would otherwise add to the CI log.\n\nI ran `ci/ci.sh` as the new rows do, with clang on an Apple M5 (macOS, no Docker): order 7 takes 15 s and order 199 takes 230 s, both including the build. I did not run the job on GitHub Actions or on Linux.\n\n*Assisted-by: my usual tools (LLM, Internet, computer). Mistakes are mine.*\n",
